{"text": "Cascade Behavioral & Occupational Health, PLLC\n2811 Colby Avenue, Suite 300 · Everett, WA 98201 · Tel 425-555-0155 · Fax 425-555-0156\nApril 28, 2026\nBeatriz Almeida-Novak, HR Business Partner\nTidemark Aerospace Components Inc.\n9000 Airport Road, Bldg 4\nMukilteo, WA 98275\nRe: Min-jun Seo (also known at work as \"Daniel Seo\"), Employee No. TAC-118824, DOB 11/23/1988\nDisability claim: Sound Mutual Life & Disability, claim no. STD-2026-0417733\nDear Ms. Almeida-Novak:\nI am a licensed clinical psychologist and have treated Mr. Seo since January 12, 2026. He has signed a release allowing me to share the information below, and only this information, with his employer. This letter accompanies the completed Form WH-380-E and is intended to meet the certification requirements of 29 C.F.R. § 825.306 and to support his request for reasonable accommodation under the ADA.\nCondition\nMr. Seo has post-traumatic stress disorder and attention-deficit/hyperactivity disorder, combined presentation, each diagnosed under DSM-5 criteria. The first is related to his service as an Army combat medic between 2009 and 2014. Both conditions are chronic. They substantially limit concentration and sleep and, during flare-ups, his ability to tolerate sudden loud noise. He currently takes prazosin 2 mg at bedtime and extended-release methylphenidate 36 mg each morning, and attends therapy weekly.\nFunctional limitations and requested accommodations\nMr. Seo can perform all essential functions of his position as a quality inspector with the following adjustments:\nReassignment from the stamping bay to an inspection station away from the drop hammers, or active noise-cancelling hearing protection that still meets plant safety rules\nA fixed day shift; rotating to nights has repeatedly disrupted his sleep and triggered symptoms\nPermission to bring his trained service dog to the administrative building for meetings; the dog would not enter the production floor\nWritten rather than verbal-only instructions for changes to inspection plans\nLeave\nHe will need intermittent leave for treatment and for flare-ups. I estimate one half-day per week for appointments, normally Monday afternoons, and one to two full days per month for episodes that cannot be predicted. He was fully unable to work from March 9, 2026 through March 27, 2026 and was admitted for three nights to a crisis stabilization unit during that period. I expect the need for intermittent leave to continue for at least twelve months, after which I will reassess.\nOther\nMr. Seo's spouse, Grace Seo, is his emergency contact and may be called at (425) 555-0198 if he becomes distressed at work. Please do not contact family members for any other purpose. Questions about this letter may be sent to me at dr.okwuosa-laurent@cascadeboh.example; I can discuss only what is written here.\nSincerely,\nSimone Okwuosa-Laurent, PsyD\nLicensed Psychologist, Washington license no. PY60448127\nNPI 1913266569\ncc: patient, by secure message", "kind": "Word document", "detail": "452 words", "notes": [], "names": {"people": ["Beatriz Almeida-Novak", "Min-jun Seo", "Daniel Seo", "Grace Seo", "Simone Okwuosa-Laurent"], "companies": ["Cascade Behavioral & Occupational Health, PLLC", "Tidemark Aerospace Components Inc.", "Sound Mutual Life & Disability"]}, "topics": {"places": ["Everett", "Mukilteo"], "health": ["post-traumatic stress disorder", "attention-deficit/hyperactivity disorder", "chronic", "sleep", "prazosin", "methylphenidate", "therapy", "crisis stabilization unit"], "sensitive": ["marital status"], "names": ["Beatriz", "Min-jun", "Daniel", "Grace", "Simone", "okwuosa-laurent", "Lawrence"]}, "judged": {"candidates": 0, "requests": 0, "failures": 0, "places": [], "labels": {}}, "chunks": 1, "chunkErrors": 0, "topicErrors": 0, "importMs": 1, "modelMs": 0, "topicMs": 0, "detectors": ["email", "url", "ip", "iban", "card", "card_exp", "cvv", "ssn", "bn_ca", "sin_ca", "ein", "card_partial", "phone", "str